The ArbitraryInteger class does not handle negative exponents correctly The result should be '-1', but is '1' instead.

```
// Given
$int =  new ArbitraryInteger('-1');

 // When
$pow = $int->pow('-1');

// Then
$this->assertSame('-1', (string) $pow);
```

I think it's a failure in the FullIntDiv function, this function also appears to not handle negative integers correctly.
